[{"code":"top_level_record_changed","severity":"error","span":{"file":"Main.beni","start":{"line":40,"col":25},"end":{"line":40,"col":36}},"title":"TOP-LEVEL RECORD CHANGED","message":"`update` changes the record at `msg#Go.0` in place, but when the program starts\nit is `origin`, a top-level value.\n\n40|main = Browser.mountAt (Tea.sandbox { init = λ⊤ → { n = 5 }, update = update, view = view }) \"root\"\n                           ^^^^^^^^^^^ the runtime hands `update` the model here\n\n16|origin = { x = 0 }\n   ^^^^^^ the top-level record is defined here\n\nA top-level value is shared by every part of the program and never changes:\nchanged in place, it would change for every part that reads it.\n\nBuild the value inside `init ⊤`, so that each call makes a fresh record:\n\n    init ⊤ = …\n\nCall that function where the model is made. Wrapping `origin` in `λ⊤ → origin`\nstill returns the same shared value.\n\nThis is the language's rule for top-level values, whether or not anything else\nreads the record. `init` builds its model; a top-level value it returns is still\nshared (ownership-checker.md §31.8)."}]
